"almafeta@gmail.com" <almafeta@gmail.com> wrote:
> Doug Freyburger wrote:
>> Nethack is written with an alphabet-style written system in mind,
>> so how well it would translate into Chinese I can't guess.  It
>> might be easier to port to Arabic than Mandarin.
>
> Easy or not, an Arabic port would be awesome.

Sure it would. Every properly translated version of nethack would be.

Speaking of properly translated ...

Can somebody of Japanese or Spanish mother tongue comment on the
quality of the grammar and the text of jnethack or spanish-nethack?

I don't want to belittle Ray Chasons achievement. As far as I can
judge he's done a wonderful job.

But one hard rule when doing translations is that you never translate
*to* a foreign language. You should always translate *from* a foreign
language *to* your native language. 

It would also be very interesting to know, how many people are playing
the translated versions and how many are native speakers and how many
play it to practice the foreign language. Although that is probably
hard to estimate.

